==================================================
2. TARGET TEAM SELECTION
==================================================

The target-team dropdown must:

- Exclude the current team.
- Show only active teams.
- Show only teams the authorized user is allowed to manage or transfer goals into.
- Prevent selecting archived, deleted, unauthorized, or inaccessible teams.
- Avoid duplicate team entries.
- Support search when there are many teams.
- Show loading, empty, and error states.

Do not rely only on UI filtering.

The backend must independently verify that the selected target team is valid and authorized.

==================================================
3. OWNER AND TEAM-MEMBERSHIP VALIDATION
==================================================

The current goal owner must be a valid member of the target team.

Before transfer, verify:

- The goal has a valid owner.
- The owner is an active user.
- The owner is a member of the target team.
- The owner has a role that permits them to own a goal in that team, according to existing rules.

When the current owner belongs to the target team:

- Allow the goal to retain the same owner.

When the current owner does not belong to the target team:

- Do not silently transfer the goal.
- Do not silently add the owner to the team.
- Do not silently change ownership.

Show a clear message:

“The current goal owner is not a member of the selected team. Select another eligible owner or add the current owner to the target team before transferring this goal.”

If existing business logic allows changing the owner during transfer, provide an “Owner” dropdown containing only eligible target-team members.

If owner reassignment during transfer is not currently supported or has not been approved, block the transfer and explain the issue.

Use the safest existing business rule. Do not invent new role behaviour.

==================================================
4. GOAL-LEVEL VALIDATION
==================================================

Goal levels may be configured differently for each team.

When the target team is selected:

- Fetch the target team’s allowed goal levels.
- Check whether the goal’s current level is allowed for the target team.
- Preserve the current level when it is valid for the target team.
- Do not silently replace the level.

When the current level is not valid for the target team:

- Require the authorized user to select a compatible goal level.
- Show only goal levels enabled for the target team.
- Disable the Transfer button until a valid level is selected.

Show a clear message:

“The current goal level is not enabled for the selected team. Select a valid level before transferring.”

The backend must reject any invalid team-and-goal-level combination even when the API is called directly.

==================================================
5. PUBLIC/PRIVATE VISIBILITY
==================================================

Preserve the goal’s existing public/private visibility during transfer unless the user explicitly changes it through an approved workflow.

Validate the behaviour of:

- Public goals
- Private goals
- Team-only goals
- Shared goals
- Goals visible through organization-level views

After transfer:

- Public goals should continue following public-goal visibility rules.
- Private goals must not become visible to unauthorized users.
- Members of the previous team must not retain access only because the goal previously belonged to their team.
- Members of the target team should receive access according to existing visibility and permission rules.
- Do not accidentally display the goal in both the old and new team due to stale mappings or cached data.

